<title>SINGAPORE: ST Aerospace in Philippine deal.</title>
<headline>ST Aerospace in Philippine deal.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore Technologies Aerospace (STA) said on Friday that, with Changi International Airport Services (CIAS), it had agreed to invest in a company to provide airport ground handling services in the Philippines.</p>
<p>STA and CIAS will invest Singapore $1.6 million for a 40 percent stake in Orbit Air Systems to provide ground handling services at Manila's international airport.</p>
<p>The rest of Orbit is held by Friendship Holdings Inc, a company formed by a group of Filipino investors led by businessman Eusebio Tanco, said the statement.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
